content/animate_objects.json:9:  "description": "Objects animate at your command. Choose a number of nonmagical objects within range that aren't being worn or carried, aren't fixed to a surface, and aren't Gargantuan. The maximum number equals your spellcasting ability modifier (Medium or smaller = 1, Large = 2, Huge = 3). Each target becomes an Animated Object Construct under your control until the spell ends or it drops to 0 HP. Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell within 500 feet.",
content/arcane_lock.json:9:  "description": "You touch a closed door, window, gate, container, or hatch and magically lock it for the duration. This lock can't be unlocked by any nonmagical means. You and any creatures you designate when you cast the spell can open and close the object despite the lock. You can also set a password that, when spoken within 5 feet of the object, unlocks it for 1 minute.",
content/burning_hands.json:3:  "id": "burning_hands",
content/burning_hands.json:9:  "description": "A thin sheet of flames shoots forth from you. Each creature in a 15-foot Cone makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Flammable objects in the Cone that aren't being worn or carried start burning. Higher slot: damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1.",
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:11:> "A flammable object hit by this spell starts burning if it isn't being worn or carried."
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:16:- `Attachment` can point at a generic `target`, but there is no way to constrain a branch to objects, much less flammable objects that are not worn or carried.
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:17:- The tracer has no atom for igniting an object or applying a burning hazard/state.
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:19:This is best classified as `atom_widening`, not `structural_widening`, because the unit's main family already exists and traces correctly. The widening pressure is a missing ignition/burning concept inside an existing activation phase.
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:23:- new surface `Effect` variant for object ignition, such as `ignite_object`
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:25:- optional target filter fields if the prototype wants to preserve the SRD restriction that only flammable objects not being worn or carried can be ignited
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:30:- target class: object only
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:31:- predicate: flammable and not worn/carried
../2735462-fire_bolt/proposal-fire_bolt.md:32:- outcome: object begins burning
